    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **254 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreCountsNamesakes`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `namesakeCount` field to owners, computed at creation time as the number of pre-existing owners sharing the same firstName + lastName (case-insensitively), persisted with the owner, and returned on GET.\n\nChanges made, following the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in AGENTS.md:\n\n1. **New pipeline function** \u2014 `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount.java`: reads the built `@Val Owner`, counts existing owners with a case-insensitive match on both first and last name via `OwnerRepository.findAll()` (the new owner isn't saved yet, so it never counts itself), and mutates the entity in place so the value is persisted.\n\n2. **Wired into the POST pipeline** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`: inserted `assignNamesakeCount` (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `assignCustomerCode` and `save`, mirroring the sibling `Assign*` steps.\n\n3. **Entity** \u2014 `Owner.java`: added `Integer namesakeCount` mapped to a `namesake_count` column, with getter/setter (MapStruct maps it into the DTO automatically by name, like `customerCode`/`householdId`).\n\n4. **API contract** \u2014 `openapi.yml`: added a read-only `namesakeCount` (int32, min 0) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n\n5. **Schema/seed** \u2014 added the `namesake_count INTEGER` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres), and appended a trailing `NULL` to the 10 column-less owner seed rows in the hsqldb `data.sql` (the test profile) so the INSERTs still match the widened table.\n\nThe acceptance test creates two owners with the same name but different postcodes (avoiding a household 409), then GETs the second and confirms `namesakeCount == 1`.",
